---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/data';
const discord = 'https://discord.gg/CRYk3uDPVt';
---
<Layout title="Official servers" description="Join the Towns & Kingdoms community, find connection details and prepare for multiplayer.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Community / Multiplayer</p>
  <h1>Find a world to call home.</h1>
  <p class="intro">A shared settlement starts with the right people. The official Discord is the place to arrange server access, find the connection details and choose a server that suits your region.</p>
  <div class="button-row"><a class="button button-primary" href={discord} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the official Discord</a><a class="button" href={href('guides/server-setup/')}>Host your own world →</a></div>
  <nav class="toc-inline" aria-label="Server guide sections"><a href="#joining">Joining</a><a href="#availability">Availability</a><a href="#shared-worlds">Shared worlds</a><a href="#connection-help">Connection help</a></nav>
  <div class="prose">
    <section id="joining"><h2>Before you connect</h2><ol><li><strong>Check the edition.</strong> Install Towns & Kingdoms 3: Beyond the Forge. A Towns & Kingdoms 2 installation has a different Minecraft version and mod list.</li><li><strong>Confirm the server’s pack file.</strong> Match its required content mods, configuration and KubeJS files. Keep a separate instance for another server’s installation.</li><li><strong>Get the address from the community.</strong> Follow the official Discord’s server-access instructions and use the address provided there.</li><li><strong>Read the joining rules.</strong> Check the community’s guidance before choosing a building location or starting a shared project.</li></ol></section>
    <section id="availability"><h2>Availability and maintenance</h2><p>Check the official Discord for current availability, maintenance notices and access questions. A connection failure can also come from a mismatched installation; read the disconnect message before changing your client.</p><p>Ask which server is appropriate for your region, whether access is open, and which pack file to install. Keep the address and connection instructions together so you can return after an update.</p></section>
    <section id="shared-worlds"><h2>A good neighbour</h2><p>Make room for other people’s plans. Discuss nearby builds, shared resources and multiplayer fights before turning a small workshop into a large settlement.</p><ul><li>Get permission before changing another player’s build or using their equipment.</li><li>Coordinate large machines and recurring boss fights with the people around you.</li><li>Give production lines a clear stop switch and investigate machinery that causes persistent server lag.</li><li>Use the community’s rules and staff guidance for claims, PvP and shared spaces.</li></ul><p>These habits work alongside the server’s own rules; ask staff when a particular build or activity needs clarification.</p></section>
    <section id="connection-help"><h2>When joining fails</h2><p>Keep the complete disconnect message and the client’s <code>logs/latest.log</code>. For a mod-list or registry mismatch, check the installed pack file and KubeJS content on both sides. A timeout needs a different investigation from a missing-mod error.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="button" href={href('support/')}>Prepare a useful report →</a><a class="button" href={href('faq/#multiplayer')}>Multiplayer FAQ →</a></div></section>
  </div>
</Layout>
